Quoting  Janis Papanagnou  <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com>:
>David Damerell wrote:
>>A barbarian - like any character - should seek intelligence to price-ID
>>spellbooks which may be safely read.
>Could you please explain why you mention price-IDing?

Price-IDing a book tells you the spell level, which lets you know when
books can be safely read. Otherwise you have to burn holy water (if
available). Even if you are willing to bless some of your books, knowing
spell levels lets you concentrate on spells you are likely to be able to
cast.

>And you seem to be implying that even barbarians should do spellcasting.

Everyone wants one spell as early as possible for confusion purposes;
besides that, even a barbarian can potentially get a robe/HoB and change
into spellcasting gear to use some utility spells.
